+# G8 result
+
+Selected `redb`, per [MMAP-KV-CANDIDATES.md](MMAP-KV-CANDIDATES.md): it provides
+the required file-backed ordered B-tree cursors and transactions without SQL
+bytecode. `RedbCount` uses native `(parent, child)` ranges and is DAG-counting
+only. Cyclic retraction requires an SCC-aware follow-up.
+
+Hermetic release runner: `src/bin/1_mmap_kv.rs`; one process per cell, 2 GiB
+Rust gun, setup staging dropped before the timed retraction. `rss_mb` is current
+macOS task resident size after the post-tick digest scan. Every completed cell
+has `digest == oracle == 0` and `live == 0`.
+
+| nodes | engine | resident Rust MB | RSS MB | tick ms | disk MB | result |
+|---:|---|---:|---:|---:|---:|---|
+| 100,000 | redb-count | 7.007 | 30.422 | 199.041 | 16.066 | digest match |
+| 100,000 | sqlite-count | 0.108 | 32.156 | 12,654.459 | 3.359 | digest match |
+| 200,000 | sqlite-count | 0.116 | 64.859 | 20,277.980 | 6.844 | digest match |
+| 1,000,000 | redb-count | 97.175 | 354.500 | 2,051.357 | 128.504 | digest match |
+| 2,000,000 | redb-count | 194.067 | 547.844 | 4,309.811 | 257.004 | digest match |
+| 2,000,000 rerun | redb-count | 194.067 | 555.062 | 4,512.409 | 257.004 | same digest; RSS repeat |
+| 500,000 | sqlite-count | - | - | - | - | child terminated before `RESULT` under the 2 GiB gun |
+| any | dd | - | - | - | - | existing `DdReach` has an all-pairs reachability digest, not this counting-Z-set DAG oracle |
+
+The file-size series and the repeated 2m cell falsify a bounded-RSS reading for
+redb in this implementation: disk grows by 16.0x from 100k to 2m and resident
+RSS grows by 18.0x. The redb spike does not hold less resident Rust RAM than
+sqlite-count in completed cells. It is faster at 100k by about 63.6x. No
+resident-RAM conclusion against dd is reported because the available dd engine
+does not implement this counting workload, and no SQLite million-node result is
+reported because the child did not reach a digest under the stated cap.
